specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:1:# Tool Input Validation
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:8:Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:12:- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required, including its complete nested path, and never invokes the executor ([validated by: returns a rejection for missing required input without invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L51), [validated by: logs the missing required property path without input values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L75), [validated by: names the complete path for a nested missing required property](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L99), [validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:13:- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46), [validated by: logs a rejected field path and constraint without logging its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L175), [validated by: reports a root property path for a wrong-typed field](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L210)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:14:- When `input` violates an `enum` constraint, the rejection names the failing field path and the `enum` constraint without invoking the executor ([validated by: names the enum constraint when rejecting a disallowed value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L151)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md:16:- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid input and undeclared properties to the executor unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L247)).

